# JavaScript Bundle Rebuilding

This project uses bundled JavaScript files for production. After editing ANY of the source JS files listed in the globs above, you MUST rebuild the bundles.

## How to Rebuild

Run this command from the project root:

```bash
cd /Users/khoi/Desktop/TEMP/_Personal/_Cursor/_DandDy/scripts && bash build-bundles.sh
```

Or equivalently:

```bash
python3 scripts/simple_bundle.py
```

## Bundle Outputs

- `manager.bundle.js` - Used by `index.html` (Character Manager)
- `character-builder/builder.bundle.js` - Used by `character-builder/index.html`

## IMPORTANT

- **Always rebuild after editing source files** - The bundles are what actually run in production
- **Never edit the bundle files directly** - They are auto-generated and will be overwritten
- **Verify the rebuild succeeded** - Check for "Wrote bundle:" messages in output

## Minification

The bundler uses **terser** (via `npx`) for minification. Terser is an AST-based minifier that properly preserves template literals - no special workarounds needed for strings.

Old workarounds like `${' '}` for spacing are no longer necessary (but still work).

## File Watcher (Alternative)

If running `./start-dev.sh`, the bundle watcher automatically rebuilds on file changes. But when editing files outside of that workflow, manual rebuilding is required.
